          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle TPR  + \\angle RPO = 90^{\\circ} = \\angle TPR  + \\angle PTR"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.169,
            0.341,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle  RPO  = \\angle  PTR"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.195,
            0.899,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, right triangle TRP is similar to the right triangle PRO by AA similarity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.241,
            0.201,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This gives"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.364,
            0.225,
            0.789,
            0.269
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{ TP }{ PO } = \\frac{ RP }{ RO },  i.e., \\frac{ TP }{5} = \\frac{4}{3}  or   TP  = \\frac{20}{3}  cm ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.277,
            0.815,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " TP can also be found by using the Pythagoras Theorem, as follows:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.304,
            0.139,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.33,
            0.302,
            0.615,
            0.322
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{TP} = x \\quad  and  \\quad \\mathrm{TR} = y. \\quad \\mathrm{Then}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.338,
            0.327,
            0.896,
            0.348
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "x ^ { 2 } = y ^ { 2 } + 1 6 \\qquad \\mathrm { ( T a k i n g ~ r i g h t ~ \\Delta ~ P R T ) }\\tag{1}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.294,
            0.353,
            0.896,
            0.373
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "x ^ { 2 } + 5 ^ { 2 } = ( y + 3 ) ^ { 2 } \\qquad \\mathrm { ( T a k i n g ~ r i g h t ~ \\Delta ~ O P T ) }\\tag{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.379,
            0.408,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Subtracting (1) from (2), we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.336,
            0.399,
            0.644,
            0.441
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "25 = 6y - 7 \\quad  or  \\quad y = \\frac{32}{6} = \\frac{16}{3}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.464,
            0.205,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.338,
            0.448,
            0.735,
            0.492
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "x^{2}=\\left(\\frac{16}{3}\\right)^{2}+16=\\frac{16}{9}(16+9)=\\frac{16\\times25}{9}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.793,
            0.464,
            0.897,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "[From (1)]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
